From: Artem Bambalov <artembambalov1993@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] surfaceflinger: a cursor-only move skips the refresh

The platform has no frameless road for a pointer: any position change
raises eTraversalNeeded, and updateCursorAsync only delivers the
position early into the refresh that follows -- "async" means past the
composition, not past the frame. On a device whose composer shows the
pointer through the display controller's own cursor, every twitch of a
mouse therefore costs a full, empty frame: no pixels change, the GPU
and the compositing engine sit idle, and the whole pipeline wakes just
to flip an identical configuration.

A transaction state that carries nothing but a position, on a layer
whose validated composition is Cursor, is now delivered straight to
that cursor and raises no flags: nothing else changed, so there is
nothing to compose. Everything else takes the ordinary road untouched,
and that includes four doors deliberately left shut:

 - a transaction whose own flags are set: eSynchronous and eAnimation
   are commit-and-wait contracts -- the sender is promised a commit
   before the call returns, and the direct road commits nothing.

 - a transaction carrying listener callbacks: on Q the completion
   callbacks are dispatched immediately when no traversal is raised,
   and the direct road has committed nothing -- a listener would be
   told the transaction is done before it is. The ordinary road keeps
   its promises.

 - a layer whose current state is already hidden: the refresh retiring
   the cursor from the composer is on its way, and a move must not
   make the vanishing pointer twitch first.

 - any layer the hardware cursor is not showing, which asks the same
   question updateCursorPosition has always asked -- so that check now
   answers with a bool instead of being written out twice.

Rebased for Q. Three things moved underneath and were re-homed:

 - setClientStateLocked grew desiredPresentTime, listenerCallbacks,
   postTime and privileged arguments; the transaction flags are still
   not among them, so they are passed through as one more trailing
   argument, same as on P. The listener-callbacks door is closed right
   inside setClientStateLocked -- it receives the callbacks as an
   argument now, so emptiness is checked on the spot.

 - updateCursorAsync now walks mDisplays, a std::map keyed by display
   token, and skips displays without an id; the direct road walks the
   same map the same way.

 - Layer::updateCursorPosition moved to the composition engine: it
   finds its OutputLayer and reads the cursor composition from
   outputLayer->getState().hwc. The fast road iterates every display
   and calls in before the layer is guaranteed to be composited
   anywhere, so the Q-side LOG_FATAL_IF on a missing output layer
   becomes a plain false return -- for the ordinary road nothing
   changes, it only ever calls for visible layers. The state the
   function reads is switched from the drawing state to the current
   one (the fast road calls in before any commit; after a commit the
   two are equal), and getTransform() -- the composed, parent-aware
   transform of the drawing state -- is replaced by
   getActiveTransform(s): the layer's own active transform of the
   state being read. A cursor layer has no parent, so the layer's own
   transform is the whole of it, and getActiveTransform is the exact
   accessor Q's own geometry code uses on a State.

---
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.h b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.h
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.h
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.h
@@ -557,3 +557,7 @@
     void setInputWindowsFinished();
     void updateCursorAsync();
+    // mocha: a transaction state carrying nothing but a position, on a
+    // layer the hardware cursor is showing, is delivered straight to the
+    // cursor without waking a refresh. Returns whether it was.
+    bool updateCursorDirect(const sp<Layer>& layer) REQUIRES(mStateLock);
     void initScheduler(DisplayId primaryDisplayId);
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.h b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.h
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.h
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.h
@@ -592,5 +592,6 @@
                                        const Vector<ComposerState>& states);
     uint32_t setClientStateLocked(const ComposerState& composerState, int64_t desiredPresentTime,
                                   const std::vector<ListenerCallbacks>& listenerCallbacks,
-                                  int64_t postTime, bool privileged) REQUIRES(mStateLock);
+                                  int64_t postTime, bool privileged, uint32_t txFlags)
+            REQUIRES(mStateLock);
     uint32_t setDisplayStateLocked(const DisplayState& s) REQUIRES(mStateLock);
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
@@ -3013,4 +3013,25 @@
     }
 }
+bool SurfaceFlinger::updateCursorDirect(const sp<Layer>& layer)
+{
+    // A hide already sits in the current state: the refresh that retires
+    // the cursor from the composer is on its way, and a move must not make
+    // the vanishing pointer twitch first.
+    if (layer->getCurrentState().flags & layer_state_t::eLayerHidden) {
+        return false;
+    }
+
+    bool applied = false;
+    for (const auto& [token, display] : mDisplays) {
+        if (!display->getId()) {
+            continue;
+        }
+
+        if (layer->updateCursorPosition(display)) {
+            applied = true;
+        }
+    }
+    return applied;
+}
 
 void SurfaceFlinger::latchAndReleaseBuffer(const sp<Layer>& layer) {
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
@@ -3849,5 +3849,5 @@
     uint32_t clientStateFlags = 0;
     for (const ComposerState& state : states) {
-        clientStateFlags |= setClientStateLocked(state, desiredPresentTime, listenerCallbacks,
-                                                 postTime, privileged);
+        clientStateFlags |= setClientStateLocked(state, desiredPresentTime, listenerCallbacks,
+                                                 postTime, privileged, flags);
     }
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
@@ -4006,4 +4006,16 @@
         if (layer->setPosition(s.x, s.y, !geometryAppliesWithResize)) {
-            flags |= eTraversalNeeded;
+            // mocha: a state that carries nothing but a position, on a layer
+            // the hardware cursor is showing, goes straight to the cursor --
+            // nothing else changed, so there is nothing to compose, and the
+            // pointer moves at its own rate. Only when the transaction as a
+            // whole promises nothing more: eSynchronous and eAnimation are
+            // commit-and-wait contracts the direct road does not honour, and
+            // a transaction with listener callbacks must take the ordinary
+            // road too -- Q dispatches those immediately when no traversal
+            // is raised, and the direct road commits nothing.
+            if (what != layer_state_t::ePositionChanged || txFlags != 0 ||
+                !listenerCallbacks.empty() || !updateCursorDirect(layer)) {
+                flags |= eTraversalNeeded;
+            }
         }
     }
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.h b/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.h
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.h
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.h
@@ -493,4 +493,6 @@
     bool getClearClientTarget(const sp<const DisplayDevice>& display) const;
-    void updateCursorPosition(const sp<const DisplayDevice>& display);
+    // Returns whether the layer is a validated hardware cursor on that
+    // display and its position was therefore delivered to the composer.
+    bool updateCursorPosition(const sp<const DisplayDevice>& display);
 
     virtual bool shouldPresentNow(nsecs_t /*expectedPresentTime*/) const { return false; }
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp
@@ -480,15 +480,23 @@
 void Layer::updateCursorPosition(const sp<const DisplayDevice>& display) {
     const auto outputLayer = findOutputLayerForDisplay(display);
-    LOG_FATAL_IF(!outputLayer);
+    // mocha: the cursor-only fast road iterates every display and calls in
+    // before the layer is guaranteed to be composited, so an absent output
+    // layer is a normal answer here, not a programming error.
+    if (!outputLayer) {
+        return false;
+    }
 
     if (!outputLayer->getState().hwc ||
         (*outputLayer->getState().hwc).hwcCompositionType !=
                 Hwc2::IComposerClient::Composition::CURSOR) {
-        return;
+        return false;
     }
 
     // This gives us only the "orientation" component of the transform
-    const State& s(getDrawingState());
+    // mocha: the current state, not the committed one -- the cursor-only
+    // fast road calls in before any commit runs, and after a commit the
+    // two are the same. Everything else below reads this state too.
+    const State& s(getCurrentState());
 
     // Apply the layer's transform, followed by the display's global transform
     // Here we're guaranteed that the layer's transform preserves rects
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp
@@ -496,5 +496,10 @@
     // Subtract the transparent region and snap to the bounds
     Rect bounds = reduce(win, getActiveTransparentRegion(s));
-    Rect frame(getTransform().transform(bounds));
+    // mocha: the current state's own active transform, not the composed
+    // drawing-state one -- the fast road calls in before any commit, and a
+    // cursor layer has no parent, so the layer's own transform is the whole
+    // of it. getActiveTransform is the accessor Q's own geometry code uses
+    // on a State.
+    Rect frame(getActiveTransform(s).transform(bounds));
     frame.intersect(display->getViewport(), &frame);
     auto& displayTransform = display->getTransform();
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/Layer.cpp
@@ -505,6 +505,7 @@
     ALOGE_IF(error != HWC2::Error::None,
              "[%s] Failed to set cursor position "
              "to (%d, %d): %s (%d)",
              mName.string(), position.left, position.top, to_string(error).c_str(),
              static_cast<int32_t>(error));
+    return true;
 }
